  <div class="legal">
    <h1>Content &amp; Copyright Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: August 28, 2026</p>

    <p>Learn with me hosts original learning content (such as Gosu queries and tutorials) alongside reference and downloadable material. This policy explains how content is handled and what is expected from users.</p>

    <h2>Copyright &amp; Ownership</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>All original learning content is provided for authorized, internal reference and learning. You may not republish, resell, or redistribute library contents to parties without authorized access.</li>
      <li>PDFs, restricted reference materials, and other study resources are made available for study only and are not to be repackaged or shared externally.</li>
      <li>If you believe content infringes your copyright, please contact us at <a href="mailto:learnwithmegw@gmail.com">learnwithmegw@gmail.com</a> with a description of the work and the location (URL/path) within the library. We will review and, where appropriate, remove or restrict access.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>User-Generated Content &amp; Discussions</h2>
    <p>Each content item may have attached discussions (questions and replies). By posting, you agree to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Be respectful and on-topic; no harassment, hate speech, or spam.</li>
      <li>Post only content you have the right to share; do not post copyrighted text, exam answers, or private data belonging to others.</li>
      <li>Not attempt to bypass access controls or share restricted/private content outside the library.</li>
      <li>Understand that discussion visibility is moderated; administrators may hide or remove content that violates this policy.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Your identity is shown as <strong>Anonymous</strong> to other users; administrators can see the author for moderation.</p>

    <h2>Restricted / Private Content</h2>
    <p>Some folders may be marked private or restricted (for example, internal or HIDDEN_FOLDERS). Such content is never used for advertising and remains accessible only to authorized roles. Ad eligibility is determined server-side and cannot be overridden from the client.</p>

    <h2>Advertising Separation</h2>
    <p>When advertising is eventually enabled, it will only appear on original learning content for eligible users. The following will remain ad-free:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>PDFs, restricted reference materials, and related study resources</li>
      <li>Restricted or private folders</li>
      <li>OWNER and ADMIN sessions</li>
      <li>Login, authentication, and error pages</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reporting &amp; Contact</h2>
    <p>To report a copyright concern, a discussion violation, or any other content issue, email <a href="mailto:learnwithmegw@gmail.com">learnwithmegw@gmail.com</a>. Include the content path or discussion URL and a brief description. We aim to review reports promptly.</p>

    <p class="muted">This policy supplements the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>. Continued use of the library after an update means you accept the updated policy.</p>
  </div>
